<div class="ccu ccu-section" data-theme="<?=ccu_h($ccu_theme)?>">
<div class="ccu-section-head">
<div class="ccu-section-copy">
<h3 class="ccu-section-title"><?=ccu_icon('shield')?>_(Permissions)_</h3>
<p class="ccu-section-desc">Your own permission rules, kept on the flash drive and loaded into every session as a managed drop-in. <code>allow</code> rules run without a prompt, <code>ask</code> rules always prompt, <code>deny</code> rules are refused. Everything here is additive: what the baseline locks (Manual mode, no bypass mode, the catastrophic-command deny list, the guard and audit hooks) is reported and ignored. Saving applies to sessions started from then on; save an empty box to remove the file.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ccu-editor">
<div class="ccu-editor-meta"><span class="ccu-path">/boot/config/plugins/claude-code-unraid/policy.d/webgui.json</span><span><?if ($ccu_rule_count === null):?><?=ccu_h(trim($ccu_policy_raw) === '' ? 'no file yet' : 'not valid JSON')?><?else:?><?=(int) $ccu_rule_count?> rule<?=ccu_h($ccu_rule_count === 1 ? '' : 's')?><?endif;?></span><span>installed as <span class="ccu-path">50-user-webgui.json</span></span></div>
<textarea id="ccu_policy" rows="14" spellcheck="false" wrap="off" placeholder='{ "permissions": { "allow": [ "Bash(docker compose *)" ] } }'><?=ccu_h($ccu_policy_raw)?></textarea>
<div class="ccu-editor-actions">
<button type="button" class="ccu-btn" onclick="ccuPolicyExample()"><?=ccu_icon('example')?><span>_(Insert example)_</span></button>
<button type="button" class="ccu-btn ccu-btn-primary" onclick="ccuSavePolicy()"><?=ccu_icon('save')?><span>_(Save permissions)_</span></button>
</div>
</div>
<p class="ccu-help">Rule syntax: <code>Bash(docker compose *)</code> matches every <code>docker compose</code> command (keep the space before the <code>*</code>), <code>Bash(uptime)</code> matches exactly that command, <code>Bash</code> alone allows every shell command, <code>WebFetch(domain:docs.unraid.net)</code> allows fetching from one domain, <code>Read(./.env)</code> names a file relative to the workspace. A prompt's "Yes, and don't ask again" writes a rule into the workspace's own <code>.claude/settings.local.json</code> instead, which is fine for rules you want in one workspace only.</p>
</div>

<div class="ccu ccu-section-head" data-theme="<?=ccu_h($ccu_theme)?>">
<div class="ccu-section-copy">
<h3 class="ccu-section-title"><?=ccu_icon('info')?>_(Settings)_</h3>
<p class="ccu-section-desc">Saved to the flash drive. Apply re-renders the managed policy; a data directory change takes effect the next time the array starts. The Help button explains each setting.</p>
</div>
